cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HealthyCropping: Offline-First Crop Disease Detection for Coffee, Cacao, and Banana"
message: "If you use HealthyCropping in your research or project, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Keylor
    family-names: Pineda
    email: keylorpineda729@gmail.com
    alias: keylorpineda
repository-code: "https://github.com/keylorpineda/healthycrop"
url: "https://github.com/keylorpineda/healthycrop"
abstract: >-
  HealthyCropping is an open-source, offline-first Android application and machine
  learning pipeline that detects crop diseases in coffee, cacao, and banana from
  smartphone photos using on-device TensorFlow Lite models, provides grounded
  agronomic explanations via retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and tracks
  farms and plots.
keywords:
  - agriculture
  - plant-disease-detection
  - computer-vision
  - tensorflow-lite
  - react-native
  - expo
  - fastapi
  - offline-first
  - costa-rica
